	(text "Connect the master power switch to J602."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 67.31 101.854 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "13f94e74-c6b3-4ad1-8441-659d79a1260f")
	)
	(text "POWER_ON is an active-high signal that is used to turn on all power\nrails except for the 3V3, which will always start automatically.\n\nThe supervisor will do various checks, and only set POWER_ON high\nwhen it believes it is safe to power on the machine."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.514 146.812 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "678be9db-24e3-4cc4-8d4b-c7c4668e5448")
	)
	(text "The PGOOD outputs of the 5V and 3V3 bucks are open-drain and share\npull-ups R706 and R1003 on CAN+5V, which makes a wired-AND: no\nextra logic is needed to combine them. PGOOD goes high once both \noutputs are in regulation (1.5-2.5 ms PGOOD delay), and only then does\nU1201 (System Clocks sheet) pass the sync clock to the bucks. If either\nrail drops out of regulation, the sync clock stops and both bucks run\nunsynchronized at about 400 kHz until PGOOD returns."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 247.65 67.056 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a4269741-369d-4f97-aafb-9a7d65dbba54")
	)
	(text_box "The Power Supply pages describe power rails that are not found in the 250407 sheets, or that have been altered from the 250407 design."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
